battlefield is known for having some of  the most varied multiplayer maps of any  shooter series  some of them are close quarters perfect  for chaotic engagements  while others are super large  battlegrounds that encourage vehicular  and long range combat  in this video we're going to break down  the 12 largest battlefield maps the  franchise has to offer with the chart  that was shared on twitter by senior  dice designer  nicholas ostrand now before we dive into  the good stuff  do me a favor and sub to this channel  i'm gonna be throwing up battlefield  videos left and right in eager  anticipation for battlefield 2042  and trust me when i say there is a lot  to be excited about  let's dive in starting the list off at  number 12 is operation market garden a  battlefield 1942 map that is meant to  replicate the real historical battle  that occurred  in the netherlands you play as either  the german forces on the axis side or as  the usa on the ally side  the u.s forces start their base on an  allied airfield and take their battle  into the center of the map where the  main village is located  here's a fun fact the u.s forces are  able to spawn by  actually parachuting close to one of the  bases by a church  the allies get to utilize this aerial  combat but the axis forces have no  planes at their disposal  with extra tanks available instead  battlefield 1 is next on our list with  the sinai desert map  the map is set within the sinai  peninsula during the raid on viral  mazzar in the british sinai and  palestine campaign  some notable characteristics include the  behemoth a gameplay mechanic introduced  in battlefield 1.  for the cyanide desert map the behemoth  takes the form of an  armored train there is the rural hilltop  town of mazad  near the head of a canyon which is  composed of a network of streets  alleyways and fortifications all  surrounded by distinct adobe structures  a significant number of firefights take  place in this vicinity  looking past the town there's almost  nothing but vast  uninterrupted desert planes meaning  on-foot combat is almost guaranteed to  be a bad  idea the desert is ultimately  featureless making infantry stick out on  the horizon  like a sore thumb a perfect target for  scout class players  the map is meant to be a prime  battleground for aircrafts tanks  and especially cavalry units  another old school battlefield game  appears on the list and battlefield 2  will appear a good number of times for  having some of the franchise's largest  maps  the dragon valley was a minshan mountain  range in china  and was also vehicle based with the us  carrier being in a position for air  support but the harbor nearby for ground  troop deployment  the battles usually ended up with the  american team making long  and grueling pushes up the valley  speaking of which that valley is  incredibly narrow despite this map being  large as hell it's a very elongated  valley that goes through various river  villages  docks and capture points scattered  across the islands  dragon valley was also remade for  battlefield 4 and the recreation is  pretty cool and faithful to the original  battlefield 5's panzerstorm was the  first post-launch map  part of the overture chapter in the  tides of war expansion  the map depicts the german invasion of  belgium a tank battle on the western  front in world war ii  is meant to reflect the real life battle  of hanut the map takes on what seems  like an unremarkable agricultural area  outside of hanut and capture points are  in small isolated buildings that are  connected by dirt roads in a shallow  stream  there's a grid of vast largely open  fields that are bordered by walls beside  the original tank wreckage  the fields only slope up gradually so  there's extremely little cover between  the checkpoints meaning a lot of long  range engagements  similar to the cyanide desert the  reasoning here is to place a heavy  emphasis on vehicular combat although in  panzerstorm's case it's like  99 tanks given it the claim of being one  of the biggest ever battlefield tank  maps  since up to 17 tanks can roam the map at  once  fush pass is a large settlement of  various camps and guard posts nestled at  the base of a wide mountain ridge  there are coal mines complete with  chimney stacks near the west side of the  map  you have lookout points by the mountain  and even a power plant facility towards  the eastern side  and both the usmc and china teams start  with their home base on an airfield  the chinese airfield is in the southwest  whereas the us airfield is on the  opposite northeastern side  el alamein was a battle during the  western desert campaign between the  german forces and the british  marking a turning point in the fight for  egypt the map in the game is huge with  two main bases on each side of a giant  ridge  the control points are scattered on the  north and south alongside the ridge with  one more point in the middle of the  desert between the ridge and the allied  base  there's a strategic advantage to both  groups with the axis group on this map  being closer to the ridge point but the  allies receiving the benefit of the  desert points  as each team kind of vie for control in  navigating hostile territory as well  as factoring in the giant ridge as it  kind of dominates the region  taking the number six slot on our list  is battlefield 4's golmid railway  this map is also based on a real-life  location the golmed laza railway in  northwest  china the factions involved the russian  and chinese teams  engaged in battle set across a very  large grassy  and open area with a huge emphasis on  vehicular combat  we're talking tanks apcs jets  helicopters  you name it a few things that  distinguish this map from everything  else so far  since it is battlefield 4 means that the  map has a revolution of sorts  rather than be a decidedly one-time  event like other battlefield 4 maps  the main revolution on gold mid railway  is a mobile train that doubles down as a  capture point  the train moves only when held by a team  and slowly makes its way closer to the  team's deployment area  giving them a territorial advantage the  map has ieds that can be blown up by c4  or by following the wires to a laptop  found near roadways  and there's even an easter egg that  takes the form of a yeti  sure enough if you go to the north part  of the map and aim a rocket towards the  snowy mountain peak  you can hear a yeti scream in the  distance  [Music]  now we've reached the top 5 largest  battlefield maps of all time with the  zatar wetlands from battlefield 2  claiming the number 5 spot  the zatar wetlands serves the  battlegrounds between the usmc  and the mec the mec has its base whereas  the us forces  start on a carrier north on the water  there are airfields farms and even a  beach with a wide network of water  channels  connecting several small islands in the  center of the map  each island is connected through the  bridges and sprawls out across this  large expansive map  with plenty of capture points at areas  of interest such as  a natural gas station a village and even  a factory  this map appears in both battlefield 2  and 1942  but for here we'll focus on how highway  tampa operates in battlefield 2.  the map is located on a peninsula with  an incredibly desolate desert terrain  sprawling far out to encourage the use  of vehicles the capture points consist  of a refinery  a gas station a couple of villages two  checkpoints each in the west and south  locations of the map  and an airfield highway tampa was one of  the first free maps to be released for  battlefield 2  post launch battlefield 2 just keeps  making this list left and right and at  number 3 we got the dalian plant  the dalian plan is a large nuclear  facility that powers an electrical grid  in northern china  the map borders a large body of water  allowing for naval combat and the  terrain is fairly varied  the usmc starting point is on the uss  essex which is located east of the  mainland on the sea with  two spawn points one on the flight deck  and the other below where players can  take inflatable boats to the nearby  island or the main battleground  there are capture points at the docks  north of the large nuclear reactor  towers  as well as another dock south of the  towers where the main battle tanks can  spawn  maintenance buildings warehouses and the  main entrance are  also scattered across the region as the  pla faction tries to fight for control  from their spawn base which is set  on an airfield far west of the map  battlefield 3 has not been mentioned at  all in this list so far  but not to worry because the bandar  desert map ranks  super high at number 2. the map came  from the armored kill expansion and is a  small bay in iran  with the moderate desert central region  you've got residential areas close to  the shore  and an artillery base inland across the  desert the map has  rock outcroppings and has a large  highway running north and south  across the area there are also villages  construction sites some outposts  and another town up in the mountains  [Music]  so before people get mad at me in the  comments if we're talking pure conquest  then the bandar desert takes the throne  of being the largest battlefield map  however halvoy is by and large the  largest battlefield map in history so  far  thanks to the fact that it is the map  used for battlefield 5's firestorm mode  firestorm is the game's take on battle  royale and battle royale maps by design  needed an extremely large space to work  with  so yes hellboy is an outlier but  technically speaking it is the largest  map compare that to another large map  like hamada  and halvoy is 10 times its size there  are different types of terrain affected  by the climate  and landmarks on halvoy from industrial  sites small snow-capped towns  and even fishing villages or lake docks  the area is huge and kind of nice to  look at if you weren't being hunted down  by countless other players  it is so wild to think that despite  these maps being so  huge battlefield 2042 is expected to  have ridiculously large maps as well  we'll dive into all things battlefield  in the coming days so be sure to stick  around  but in the meanwhile let me know what  you think about battlefield's largest  map so far  thanks for watching  [Music]  you

